p_id": "step_16", "tool": "node_degree", "args": {"nodes": [641, 1465, 1583], "window": [48098, 52897]}, "result_digest": "c577b17a2707ce9f", "result_summary": "{\"nodes\": [{\"distinct_partners\": 11, \"events\": 11, \"node\": 641}, {\"distinct_partners\": 3, \"events\": 3, \"node\": 1465}, {\"distinct_partners\": 43, \"events\": 45, \"node\": 1583}], \"window\": [48098, 52897]}", "latency_ms": 3, "tokens_before": 39257, "tokens_after": 39257, "ok": true, "error": ""}], "final_claim": {"task_id": "t_44f03991", "decision": "absent", "mechanism": "cascade", "entities": [303, 1293, 28, 1438, 641, 1465, 1583], "window": [28296, 66695], "confidence": 0.6, "narrative": "303 and 1293 are each involved in only 4 events. 303 can only emit to {641,1465,1583}; 1293 can only receive from {28,1438}. The 1438->1293 contacts all precede 47497, i.e. before 303's earliest out-event in the window, so the sole candidate terminal hop is the single 28->1293 event localised to ~52598-52897. The only 303 out-event preceding it sits at ~48098-48697 (its other out-events are at >=59497, after 1293's final event). Closing that ~4000-unit gap under a 600-unit maximum per-hop delay would require seven or more chained relays, and none was evidenced. The large 2-hop neighbourhood and the high activity of hub 1583 / receiver 28 provide a static (time-ignoring) connection and high background volume, which is the confound explicitly excluded; no time-respecting 600-unit chain from 303 to 1293 is supported.", "evidence": [{"trace_id": "step_02", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_03", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_04", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_08", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_09", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_12", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_14", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_06", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_07", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_05", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_15", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_16", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_01", "role": "confounder_control"}]}, "raw_final_response": "## Analysis\n\n**Structure of the endpoints (step_02, step_03, step_04):** Both 303 and 1293 are very sparse (4 events each). 303's outgoing contacts are only {641, 1465, 1583}; 1293's only incoming contacts are {28, 1438}. So any cascade must leave 303 via 641/1465/1583 and land on 1293 via 28 or 1438.\n\n**Timing of the endpoints:**\n- 303's events (step_06, step_10, step_12, step_13): one at \u224848098\u201348697, one at \u224853048\u201353197, and two later (\u224859497\u201361896, \u224861897\u201364296).\n- 1293's events (step_07, step_11, step_14): one before 33096, two in 42697\u201347496, and one at \u224852598\u201352897. Nothing after 57096.\n\n**Which arrival could close a cascade?** step_09 shows 1438\u21921293 has *no* events after 47497 (its contacts precede all of 303's activity in the window). step_08 shows exactly one 28\u21921293 event, which must be the 1293 event localised to \u224852598\u201352897 (step_14). That is the only possible terminal hop of a cascade seeded by 303.\n\n**The gap is fatal:** the only 303 out-event that precedes this arrival occurs at \u224848098\u201348697 (step_12). The 303 later events (\u226559497) are after 1293's last event, so they cannot seed anything. Bridging \u224848.4k \u2192 \u224852.7k with per-hop delay \u2264600 would require \u22657 chained relay hops. 303's direct partners are not 28 (step_03 vs step_15), and although 1583 is a busy hub (45 events in 48098\u201352897, step_16) and 28 has 35 distinct in-contacts in that span (step_15), that volume is exactly the confound the task warns about \u2014 it establishes a *time-ignoring* connection, not a chain of \u2264600-unit steps. No evidence of an unbroken relay chain was found, and the required latency is ~7\u00d7 the allowed inter-event gap.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_44f03991\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [303, 1293, 28, 1438, 641, 1465, 1583],\n  \"window\": [28296, 66695],\n  \"confidence\": 0.6,\n  \"narrative\": \"303 and 1293 are each involved in only 4 events. 303 can only emit to {641,1465,1583}; 1293 can only receive from {28,1438}. The 1438->1293 contacts all precede 47497, i.e. before 303's earliest out-event in the window, so the sole candidate terminal hop is the single 28->1293 event localised to ~52598-52897. The only 303 out-event preceding it sits at ~48098-48697 (its other out-events are at >=59497, after 1293's final event). Closing that ~4000-unit gap under a 600-unit maximum per-hop delay would require seven or more chained relays, and none was evidenced. The large 2-hop neighbourhood and the high activity of hub 1583 / receiver 28 provide a static (time-ignoring) connection and high background volume, which is the confound explicitly excluded; no time-respecting 600-unit chain from 303 to 1293 is supported.\",\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_14\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_15\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_16\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ]\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 47775, "total_output_tokens": 7226, "total_tokens": 55001, "total_latency_ms": 101338, "llm_calls": 8, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error"